  "findings": [
    {
      "issue": "Putting workers in the orchestrator's own pane removes the separation the ownership check relied on. `owned()` (lib/agent.js:109) scopes workers by (workspace, orchestratorPane), and `context()` (lib/agent.js:101) takes the caller's pane from `cmux identify`. Before this branch a Codex/Claude worker ran in a separate workers pane, so `acs-agent` run from inside a worker was refused with 'worker belongs to another orchestrator'. Now a non-Grok worker is a tab in ctx.pane, so its own `acs-agent list/send/close/answer/wait` calls pass `owned()` for every sibling worker, and an `acs-agent open` from a worker is recorded as the orchestrator's (same orchestratorPane) and opens another tab in the orchestrator's pane.",
      "file": "lib/agent.js",
      "line": "574",
      "quote": "const place = vendor === 'grok' ? ['new-pane', '--direction', 'right'] : ['new-surface', '--pane', ctx.pane];",
      "suggestion": "Scope ownership by something a worker tab does not share with the orchestrator: record the orchestrator's own surface (caller.surface_ref) at open and compare it in owned(), or refuse acs-agent commands whose caller surface is a recorded worker surface.",
      "likelihood": 2,
      "impact": 5,
      "protected": false,
      "trigger": "A Claude builder worker (permission-mode auto) opened with `acs-agent open opus ...` runs `acs-agent list`, `acs-agent close <sibling id>` or `acs-agent open ...` itself, e.g. because it tries to delegate. Builders are briefed not to run other models, so this is an uncommon path.",
      "preExisting": false,
      "risk": 10,
      "severity": "low",
      "filed": true,
      "status": "verified-quote",
      "id": "f1"
    },
    {
      "issue": "ask-model reads the branch for the run file from the process's working directory, not from `--cwd`. The model call runs in `cwd = path.resolve(o.cwd ?? process.cwd())` (tools/ask-model.mjs:1197), but startWatch spawns `git branch --show-current` with no `cwd` option and falls back to `path.basename(process.cwd())`. With `--cwd` pointing at another worktree or repo, the sidebar line and the pane tab title name the caller's branch (or folder) instead of the one the model is working in, contradicting the README's 'the branch it runs on'.",
      "file": "tools/ask-model.mjs",
      "line": "222",
      "quote": "const current = git ? spawnSync(git, ['branch', '--show-current'], { encoding: 'utf8', stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'ignore'], timeout: 2000 }) : null;",
      "suggestion": "Pass the resolved cwd into startWatch and use it for both the git call (`cwd` option) and the basename fallback.",
      "likelihood": 3,
      "impact": 2,
      "protected": false,
      "trigger": "Inside cmux with watch on sidebar or pane: `ask-model --role advisor --cwd <another worktree> --prompt-file f` run from a checkout on a different branch.",
      "preExisting": false,
      "risk": 6,
      "severity": "low",
      "filed": true,
      "status": "verified-quote",
      "id": "f2"
    }
